---
import SoftBoundary from './SoftBoundary.astro';
import '../styles/women-system.css';
import {womensHealthFr as c} from '../data/womens-health-fr';
import {url} from '../data/site';
---
<div class="womens-health-page">
<section class="section feminine-hero"><div><h1>{c.title}</h1><p class="feminine-statement">{c.statement}</p><p>{c.intro}</p><a class="button" href="#approche-sante-feminine">Découvrir mon approche</a></div><div class="feminine-hero-photo"><img src="/images/softness-1200.webp" srcset="/images/softness-640.webp 640w, /images/softness-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 45vw" width="1200" height="800" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Lauriane au bord de la mer, les mains près du visage dans la lumière du coucher de soleil"/><svg class="feminine-hero-orbit" viewBox="0 0 600 600" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M573 331C596 452 484 571 347 549C243 532 215 572 191 602" stroke="#FF6230" stroke-width="9" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M504 561C456 603 403 590 372 578" stroke="#F8BCCA" stroke-width="21" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></div></section>
<section class="section feminine-why" id="approche-sante-feminine"><div class="feminine-editorial"><h2>Pourquoi la santé féminine ?</h2><div>{c.why.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}</div></div><p class="feminine-pull feminine-why-statement"><span>Comprendre ses rythmes,</span> c’est aussi comprendre son corps et tout ce qui va avec.</p></section>
<SoftBoundary from="#FFFDF7" to="#F8BCCA" intensity="network-in"/>
<section class="section feminine-cycle"><svg class="feminine-cycle-trajectory" viewBox="0 0 1440 620" preserveAspectRatio="none" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1210 -62C1455 45 1513 255 1321 369C1215 434 1181 348 1111 421C1025 511 1096 587 936 634" stroke="#FF6230" stroke-width="52" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M-75 365C126 306 211 563 438 535C578 518 672 441 793 507C824 524 845 550 863 565" stroke="#FF6230" stroke-width="25" stroke-linecap="round"/><path d="M1258 -45C1448 31 1493 214 1354 298" stroke="#5E1AF4" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="1177" cy="392" r="9" fill="#5E1AF4"/><circle cx="902" cy="589" r="7" fill="#5E1AF4"/></svg><div class="feminine-cycle-composition"><h2>Se reconnecter à son cycle</h2><div class="feminine-cycle-reading"><p>Les cycles peuvent devenir une manière d’observer son corps, ses rythmes et ses changements, et un outil de compréhension de soi.</p><p>{c.rhythms}</p></div><p class="feminine-pull">{c.nonlinear}</p></div></section>
<SoftBoundary from="#F8BCCA" to="#FFFDF7" intensity="network-out"/>
<section class="section feminine-topics"><svg class="feminine-topics-orbit" viewBox="0 0 1440 430" preserveAspectRatio="none" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1500 24C1208 -63 1035 40 1117 155C1214 292 1400 202 1470 357" stroke="#FF6230" stroke-width="10" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><h2>Les sujets que j’approfondis<span class="feminine-dot" aria-hidden="true">.</span></h2><p>{c.topicsIntro}</p><ul class="feminine-topic-grid">{c.topics.map(topic=><li id={`sujet-${topic.key}`}>{topic.title}</li>)}</ul></section>
<section class="section feminine-development"><div class="feminine-editorial"><h2>Une spécialisation en développement</h2><div><p>{c.development[0]}</p><p>Cette démarche vient enrichir ma pratique de <a class="feminine-inline-link" href={url('fr','acupuncture')}>l’acupuncture traditionnelle</a> et ma manière d’observer les liens entre le cycle, le corps et les différents signes exprimés par chaque femme.</p><aside class="feminine-note"><p class="eyebrow">{c.nextTitle}</p><p>{c.next}</p></aside></div></div></section>
<section class="final-cta section"><svg class="feminine-closing-orbit" viewBox="0 0 500 500" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M-91 25C198 -68 389 126 271 302C215 384 71 304 30 439" stroke="#FF6230" stroke-width="18" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><h2>Prendre rendez-vous<span class="feminine-dot">.</span></h2><p class="feminine-final-support">{c.whyClosing}</p><a class="button" href={url('fr','contact')}>Prendre rendez-vous</a></section>
</div>
